---
/**
 * tagForge AI SEO Generator Case Study Page
 * Purpose: Presents a high-fidelity, comprehensive case study of the tagForge AI SEO Generator system.
 * Contents: Includes project overview, executive summary, problem statement, solution details, 
 *           architectural pillars (Vercel double-prefix routing, NextAuth dynamic JWT sync, dynamic server resolution),
 *           database schemas, monetization structures, and key business benefits.
 * Fit: Part of the portfolio subpages under '/portfolio/tagforge', highlighting full-stack 
 *      monorepo engineering capabilities, serverless routing architectures, and production-ready UI design.
 */

import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'tagForge AI SEO Generator Case Study | Jun Alvior';
const description = 'A technical case study of tagForge, a premium full-stack AI-powered SEO suite built as a Next.js and Express.js monorepo with Stripe subscriptions and Google OAuth.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-grow flex flex-col">
    <!-- ORGANISMS: Project Case Study -->
    <article class="py-24 bg-grey-light dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] flex-grow transition-colors duration-300">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <a
            href="../../portfolio/"
            class="hover:text-wood-accent transition-colors flex items-center gap-1 font-medium"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
            </svg>
            Back to Portfolio
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Header -->
        <header class="mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
          <div class="mb-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl border border-gray-200/50 dark:border-gray-800/50">
            <img
              src="../../assets/tagForge.webp"
              alt="tagForge AI SEO Generator Mockup"
              class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[500px] hover:scale-101 transition-transform duration-700"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="800"
              height="450"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-950/50 text-green-700 dark:text-green-400">
              Active Project
            </span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-950/50 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100">
              Case Study
            </span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
            tagForge AI SEO Generator
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed font-normal">
            Full-Stack AI SaaS with Google Cloud Identity Synchronization and Stripe Monetization
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 mt-6">
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              Next.js 14 (App Router)
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              Express.js
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              TypeScript
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              Groq Llama-3-70B
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              NextAuth.js
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              Stripe Billing
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm transition-colors duration-300">
              MongoDB Atlas
            </span>
          </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Project Links (Top CTA) -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-16" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50">
          <a
            href="https://seo-project-21.vercel.app/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="px-6 py-3.5 bg-wood-accent hover:bg-wood-700 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 flex items-center gap-2"
          >
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" />
            </svg>
            Live Demo
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/property360-2/seo-project"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="px-6 py-3.5 bg-transparent border-2 border-wood-accent hover:bg-wood-50 dark:hover:bg-[#252528] text-wood-accent dark:text-wood-300 font-semibold rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 flex items-center gap-2"
          >
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.477 2 12c0 4.42 2.865 8.166 6.839 9.489.5.092.682-.217.682-.482 0-.237-.008-.866-.013-1.7-2.782.603-3.369-1.34-3.369-1.34-.454-1.156-1.11-1.462-1.11-1.462-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.531 1.03 1.531 1.03.892 1.529 2.341 1.087 2.91.831.092-.646.35-1.086.636-1.336-2.22-.253-4.555-1.11-4.555-4.943 0-1.091.39-1.984 1.029-2.683-.103-.253-.446-1.27.098-2.647 0 0 .84-.269 2.75 1.025A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.294 2.747-1.025 2.747-1.025.546 1.377.203 2.394.1 2.647.64.699 1.028 1.592 1.028 2.683 0 3.842-2.339 4.687-4.566 4.935.359.309.678.919.678 1.852 0 1.336-.012 2.415-.012 2.743 0 .267.18.579.688.481C19.137 20.164 22 16.418 22 12c0-5.523-4.477-10-10-10z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
            View Code
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Content Flow -->
        <div class="space-y-16">

          <!-- SECTION 0: At-a-Glance Summary -->
          <section id="summary" class="bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-5 flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wood-accent shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path>
              </svg>
              At a Glance
            </h2>
            <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-5 text-sm">
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold text-wood-accent uppercase tracking-widest text-xs">Problem</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">SEO teams manually wrote titles, descriptions, and alt text for every product page — slow and inconsistent.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold text-wood-accent uppercase tracking-widest text-xs">Role</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Designed the system architecture and implemented the frontend, REST API, authentication, billing, and deployment.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold text-wood-accent uppercase tracking-widest text-xs">Solution</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Built an AI SaaS that generates titles, meta descriptions, alt text, and keywords from product input.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold text-wood-accent uppercase tracking-widest text-xs">Result</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Generated content at 280+ tokens per second in testing, with quota-based Stripe monetization.</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="md:col-span-2">
                <dt class="font-bold text-wood-accent uppercase tracking-widest text-xs">Proof</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">Live demo, GitHub repository, screenshots, and the architecture diagram below.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </section>

          <!-- SECTION 1: Executive Summary -->
          <section id="executive-summary" class="bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border-l-4 border-wood-accent border-y border-r border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-r-2xl p-6 sm:p-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <div class="hidden sm:block text-wood-accent">
                <svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wood-accent shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"></path>
                  </svg>
                  Executive Summary
                </h2>
                <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                  <strong>tagForge</strong> is a premium AI-powered SEO SaaS application built to enable digital marketers, content creators, and SEO professionals to synthesize metadata: titles, meta descriptions, Open Graph parameters, image alternative texts, and high-relevancy keywords. 
                </p>
                <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-3">
                  By engineering a high-fidelity monorepo architecture, tagForge co-hosts a **Next.js 14 App Router frontend** and a **TypeScript Express.js REST API** inside a single, unified serverless project on Vercel. Through integrated Google Cloud OAuth (NextAuth.js), robust **Stripe payments with real-time webhooks**, and rapid inference utilizing **Groq Llama-3-70B**, the platform bypasses CORS overhead, keeps hosting costs low, and achieves SEO content generation rates of **over 280 tokens per second** in the tested setup.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- SECTION 2: The Problem vs The Solution -->
          <section id="problem-solution" class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <!-- Problem Card -->
            <div class="bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 shadow-sm rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 flex flex-col">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
                <span class="p-2 bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-950/50 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 rounded-lg">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">The Monorepo Nightmare</h3>
              </div>
              <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed flex-grow">
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-red-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Routing Collisions:</strong> Hosting Next.js and Express inside a single serverless Vercel deploy typically overlaps routes and triggers endless 404 errors.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-red-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Session Disconnection:</strong> Google OAuth on the frontend needs complex backend check-ins to sync accounts and safely issue secure custom JWT payloads.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-red-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Lambda Resolution Failures:</strong> Relative backend fetch paths fail inside isolated serverless Lambdas because no browser context is active.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-red-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Build-Time Compilation Crash:</strong> Referencing client-side dynamic search query strings in App Router roots triggers build-time static pre-rendering bails.</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Solution Card -->
            <div class="bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 shadow-sm rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 flex flex-col">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
                <span class="p-2 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-950/50 text-green-600 dark:text-green-400 rounded-lg">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">The Engineering Solution</h3>
              </div>
              <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed flex-grow">
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-green-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Double-Prefix Routing:</strong> Mapped Next.js to `/` and Express to `/_/backend` using a highly optimized `vercel.json` rewrite strategy.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-green-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>NextAuth Proxy Synchronizer:</strong> Intercepted OAuth tokens client-side, proxied registration into Mongo, and generated custom session JWTs.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-green-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>Context-Aware Resolver:</strong> Programmed a smart API client helper that detects runtime environments and resolves canonical serverless domains.</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <span class="text-green-500 font-bold">•</span>
                  <span><strong>React Suspense Encapsulation:</strong> Isolated all query hook invocations inside dynamic `&lt;Suspense&gt;` boundaries, securing clean compilations.</span>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- SECTION 3: Visual Flow Diagram -->
          <section id="architecture-flow" class="border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">tagForge SaaS System Architecture</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 relative">
              <!-- Frontend Node -->
              <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 bg-gray-50/50 dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] rounded-xl p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-between items-center shadow-sm">
                <span class="p-3 bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-950/30 text-wood-accent rounded-full mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9.75 17L9 20l-1 1h8l-1-1-.75-3M3 13h18M5 17h14a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-sm">Next.js Web Frontend</h4>
                  <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mt-1">Sleek dark interface, NextAuth credential management, and responsive dynamic dashboards.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 mt-4 pt-3 text-2xs text-wood-accent font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">
                  Next.js App Router
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Vercel Gateway Node -->
              <div class="border border-wood-100 dark:border-gray-800/60 bg-wood-50/10 dark:bg-[#1a1a1a]/50 rounded-xl p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-between items-center shadow-md ring-1 ring-wood-accent/20">
                <span class="p-3 bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-950/30 text-amber-500 rounded-full mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 7h12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l-4 4m0 6H4m0 0l4 4m-4-4l4-4" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-sm">Vercel Rewrite Router</h4>
                  <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mt-1">Multi-service double-prefix gateway translating `/` and `/_/backend` endpoints seamlessly.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 mt-4 pt-3 text-2xs text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">
                  vercel.json Mapping
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Backend Node -->
              <div class="border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 bg-gray-50/50 dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] rounded-xl p-5 text-center flex flex-col justify-between items-center shadow-sm">
                <span class="p-3 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-950/30 text-blue-500 rounded-full mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <div>
                  <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-sm">Express API & Databases</h4>
                  <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mt-1">Mongoose schemas, Stripe dynamic upgrades, and high-speed Groq Llama-3 endpoints.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 mt-4 pt-3 text-2xs text-blue-500 font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">
                  TypeScript Express API
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Subheading inside layout describing monorepo loop -->
            <div class="mt-6 text-center text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800 pt-4 flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-500 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z"></path>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Unified Single Domain:</strong> Next.js Frontend calls `/` &rarr; NextAuth intercepts Google Accounts &rarr; Node/Express synchronizes profiles on MongoDB &rarr; Subscriptions upgrade via Stripe webhooks on the same domain.</span>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- SECTION 4: Architecture Pillars -->
          <section id="architecture-pillars" class="space-y-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 pb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-wood-accent shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4M7.835 4.697a3.42 3.42 0 001.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 014.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 001.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 013.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010 4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806 1.946 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138 3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-4.438 0 3.42 3.42 0 00-1.946-.806 3.42 3.42 0 01-3.138-3.138 3.42 3.42 0 00-.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 010-4.438 3.42 3.42 0 00.806-1.946 3.42 3.42 0 013.138-3.138z"></path>
              </svg>
              Core Architecture Pillars
            </h3>
            
            <div class="space-y-6">
              <div>
                <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="w-1.5 h-6 bg-wood-accent rounded-full"></span>
                  1. Multi-Service Monorepo Configuration (`vercel.json`)
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                  To eliminate complex Multi-Domain CORS errors and maximize server deployment consolidation, we utilize Vercel's multi-service architecture within a single workspace:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li><strong>Next.js Frontend</strong> is mapped to the project root and listens on `/`, which lets client components pre-render efficiently and load fast.</li>
                  <li><strong>TypeScript Express.js API</strong> is mapped to `/backend` in the project directory, and answers queries under the prefix rewrite rules of `/_/backend/*`.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <span class="w-1.5 h-6 bg-wood-accent rounded-full"></span>
                  2. Google Cloud OAuth & Custom Backend JWT Synchronizer
                </h4>
                <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                  Integrating NextAuth on the client side with a standalone Express/MongoDB backend requires secure synchronization protocols:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li>When a user logs in via Google Cloud, NextAuth's `jwt` callback securely proxies a check-in request to the backend Express server.</li>
                  <li>If the Google account does not exist in MongoDB, the Express backend registers the user record, compiles an internal security JWT access token, and passes it back to the Next.js frontend cache, achieving unified session consistency.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

