                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"></path>
                    </svg>
                    Solving Route Resolution inside Lambda Environments
                  </h5>
                  <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                    Because relative base URLs (e.g., `/_/backend/api`) break inside headless execution paths, a dynamic helper resolves canonical locations contextually:
                  </p>
                  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                    <li>When running on the <strong>Server-side (Vercel Lambda)</strong>, the helper detects the absence of `window` and resolves absolute domains canonicalized in `NEXTAUTH_URL` (e.g. `https://seo-project-21.vercel.app/_/backend`).</li>
                    <li>When running in the <strong>Browser (client-side)</strong>, the helper uses the relative routed prefix `/_/backend` to cleanly leverage the rewrite proxy setup.</li>
                    <li>In <strong>Local Development</strong>, it falls back gracefully to `localhost:5000` to preserve developer velocity.</li>
                  </ul>
